Package: fast.string
Type: Package
Title: Fast Parallel String Functions via PCRE2 and RcppParallel
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: person("Kyle", "Haynes", email = "kyle@kylehaynes.com.au", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Depends:
    R (>= 3.5.0)
Description: Fast equivalents of grepl(), grep(), sub(), and gsub() that
    use PCRE2 for regular expressions and prepared literal search for fixed
    strings, parallelised across CPU cores via Intel TBB through
    RcppParallel. Also provides byte- and Unicode-aware string similarities,
    edit distances, q-gram set and cosine similarity, phonetic blocking keys
    (Soundex, Refined Soundex, NYSIIS, Cologne, Double Metaphone,
    Caverphone), fixed-format date and timestamp parsing, and
    memory-efficient top-N fuzzy lookup without allocating a full comparison
    matrix. Includes a reproducible benchmark harness for measuring
    workload- and platform-specific performance.
